rs/jcostello/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T17:56:02Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T17:57:15Z","body":"> That should be disclosed clearly, was it just things like that or other code changes?\r\n\r\nI will edit the disclose. I just used to point me out unused stuff. Just before pushing to ensure everything is fine","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5498132212/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5796586627","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123078#issuecomment-5796586627","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123078","id":5796586627,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWYDkgw","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-23T14:22:54Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T16:06:14Z","body":"Tested and works as expected. This is absolutely perfect to easily and quickly validate lightmap UVs. In my opinion the colors can be more saturated though, especially since these colors are influenced by the tonemapper and are even less saturated when using AGX.\r\n\r\n| | w/o selection | w/ selection |\r\n| - | - | - |\r\n| Linear | <img width=\"1167\" height=\"915\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc52eed6-7c30-4623-b9d2-114994a7c5ec\" /> | <img width=\"1167\" height=\"915\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52e98ace-e622-4614-bdc3-2fbc1df35e32\" /> |\r\n| AGX | <img width=\"1167\" height=\"915\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/12967391-b436-406e-896b-242c2a16b344\" /> | <img width=\"1167\" height=\"915\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e8b96b76-ecaa-47f0-b28d-2df8409a9fb9\" /> |\r\n\r\nI think we should just go full saturation on these. I think this gives a more immediate clear read, and allows you to more easily and quickly spot potential problematic areas. I also believe that for people with colorblindness the low color contrast could be an issue.\r\n| | w/o selection | w/ selection |\r\n| - | - | - |\r\n| Linear | <img width=\"1173\" height=\"920\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/885ebbef-2642-46ec-a502-903c2f13e3d6\" /> | <img width=\"1173\" height=\"920\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8d27272a-8d56-43e9-8135-44c514e4d4af\" /> |\r\n| AGX | <img width=\"1173\" height=\"920\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a0dc5601-805d-431b-8ee3-e09be889a084\" /> | <img width=\"1173\" height=\"920\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a870dee3-a52b-4e74-936b-68ec3872dc26\" /> |\r\n\r\n(For reference these are those increased saturation colors)\r\n```\r\n\tvec3 below_color = vec3(0.0, 0.0, 0.9);\r\n\tvec3 target_color = vec3(0.0, 0.9, 0.1);\r\n\tvec3 above_color = mix(vec3(1.0, 0.2, 0.0), vec3(0.7, 0.0, 0.0), smoothstep(1.0, 4.0, relative_log));\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI'm wondering if the target texel density setting makes more sense as a project setting instead, and if this view should be toggled in the perspective menu instead of in the toolbar. I don't immediately recall anywhere else where we toggle a debug view from the toolbar. Especially since this debug view stays active even when you don't have the lightmapGI node selected, meaning that this toolbar button stays present even though you're not explicitly in the lightmapGI node context anymore.\r\n\r\nMy intuition would be to place a toggle for this view here or under the `Display Advanced...` dropdown.\r\n<img width=\"375\" height=\"745\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e8b653d9-6730-4976-89f3-13e38b19f254\" />\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5796586627/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5798160336","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123078#issuecomment-5798160336","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123078","id":5798160336,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWZjn0A","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:59:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T15:59:42Z","body":"> In my opinion the colors can be more saturated though, especially since these colors are influenced by the tonemapper and are even less saturated when using AGX.\r\n\r\nThis begs the question of whether tonemapper/exposure settings should even have an effect when using any of the debug draw modes. I also mentioned this in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116446#pullrequestreview-3834705942, so it's not exclusive to this new debug draw mode.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5798160336/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5798423459","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123078#issuecomment-5798423459","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123078","id":5798423459,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWZzrow","user":{"login":"jcostello","id":1168582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjg1ODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1168582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello","html_url":"https://github.com/jcostello","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-23T16:16:04Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T16:16:04Z","body":"I think we can crank the saturation a bit more and unsaturated the non-selected meshes to have that contrast, but only as a patch for having the tonemap applied.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, to keeps this simple, this is part of the lightmap editor plugin, therefore it can't be a debug view. The contextual menu next to it should be, IMO, lightmap based and not a project setting, so this allow different lightmaps in the scene to have different texel targets,  but that is just my opinion. I can change it to a project setting if most of the people agreed to.\r\n\r\nLocally I tested to display this under the unshaded debug view and also make the wireframe, overview and unshaded view to compensate the exposure, so no matter the exposure in the scene, the brightness is the same, but that is for another PR I guess.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5798423459/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]